---
description: >
  Brevity-sweep audit of `src/tools/inspect/.aide` — frontmatter close to caps; 6 desired outcomes (cap 4) including a long MCP-tool-description meta-outcome that enumerates exact file extensions and exact return-field names.
intent: >
  aide_inspect is the symbol-introspection tool. Spec is mostly bounded
  but `outcomes.desired[5]` is a description-vs-handler-drift meta-outcome
  that enumerates exact return-field shape, supported file extensions, and
  optional-parameter naming — forbidden content saturating one outcome.
misalignment:
  - spec-bloat
---

## Issues

- [ ] `description` is 108 chars (under cap, fine).

- [ ] `intent` is 92 words (under cap 100, fine).

- [ ] `outcomes.desired` has 6 items (cap 4). Items 0 and 5 carry the same
  return-shape contract ("returns kind, file, line, signature, jsdoc"); item
  5 is a meta-outcome about the MCP tool description with exhaustive enumeration
  of return fields, supported extensions (`ts`, `tsx`, `js`, `jsx`, `mjs`,
  `cjs`), and optional-parameter rules. Most of this is unit-test territory
  (description-vs-handler-drift detection is naturally a unit test on the
  registered description).
  Traces to: `outcomes.desired` | Brevity Contract caps + outcomes-purpose test + Forbidden content (file extensions, exact strings)
  Misalignment: spec-bloat
  Category: Brevity, Forbidden-content

- [ ] `outcomes.undesired` has 5 paragraph-length items including the MCP-tool-description
  drift meta-rule (item 4) which restates item 5 of desired. Compress to
  3-4 falsifiable failure modes.
  Traces to: `outcomes.undesired` | Brevity Contract caps + Forbidden content (file extensions, function names)
  Misalignment: spec-bloat
  Category: Brevity, Forbidden-content

- [ ] No body sections at all (no `## Context`, `## Strategy`, `## Good
  examples`, `## Bad examples`, `## References`). The Brevity Contract
  requires the five body sections. This is a structural spec gap, not bloat
  per se — though the absence is what's letting the frontmatter carry all
  the weight that should be in body.
  Traces to: body section completeness | spec-gap (missing required body sections)
  Misalignment: spec-gap
  Category: structural-gap

- [ ] Carry-forward (prior cycle): 0 unchecked items (existing todo's items
  are checked).

## Retro

aide_inspect's bloat is concentrated in one meta-outcome that tries to
enforce description-vs-handler-drift detection at the spec level. That's a
unit-test concern; the spec should commit to "the agent reads the registered
MCP description and gets the same expectations as a reader of this spec"
without enumerating the contract surface byte-for-byte.

The structural gap (no body sections) means an aligner walking the tree gets
no Strategy or examples on this leaf — the spec exists as frontmatter only.
The fix is to add the five body sections, each within caps, and let them
carry the spec's shape; the meta-outcome about description drift collapses
into a single Strategy paragraph naming the contract surface.
